  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 210 PM MDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\nIt will be a very pleasant Fall weekend around the region with highs \nwithin a few degrees of seasonal averages and mostly clear skies. A \nridge will amplify over the Intermountain West over the weekend, \neventually retrograding over the Mojave desert as northwest flow \ndevelops over The Great Basin.\n\nModels are still in relatively poor agreement about the passage of a \nfast moving shortwave trough over the southern Rockies \nTuesday/Wednesday of next week, although the trend has been towards \na less amplified feature and drier conditions overall. Low rain \nchances are still in the forecast, but all ensembles have trended \ndrier, even the GEFS which has been the most bullish about a deeper \ntrough. Ridging is forecast to remain in place over the southwest US \nmid to late week, with high confidence that the dry weather will \ncontinue through at least the end of the workweek. Temperatures will \ngradually be climbing as well, reaching slightly above normal by the \nend of the week.",
